Gaster enters PwnedDFU mode on Apple devices with A5-A11 SoCs using
the checkm8 boot ROM exploit. In PwnedDFU the boot ROM accepts unsigned
images, which is the entry point for booting alternative operating
systems from a host over USB.

The phone rescue kit uses it to give unsupported Apple phones a second
life with EmberBSD. Exploitation runs entirely in RAM: gaster never
writes to device storage.

This package builds the portable libusb backend with the pre-generated
boot ROM payload headers from files/.
